                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Pittsburgh PA",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 20 at 11:42AM EDT until September 20 at 1:30PM EDT by NWS Pittsburgh PA",
                "description": "At 1142 AM EDT, Soppler radar indicated that rain was ending across\nthe warned area. Earlier, emergency management reported several\ninstances of flash flooding across the warned area. Between 1.5 and\n2.5 inches of rain have fallen. Additional rainfall amounts up to 1.0\ninch are possible in the warned area. Flash flooding is already\noccurring.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by heavy rain.\n\nSOURCE...Emergency management reported.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nWashington, Canonsburg, Avella, Wolfdale, McGovern, Bentleyville,\nEast Washington, New Eagle, Baidland, Houston, Ellsworth,\nClaysville, Deemston, Eighty Four, Cokeburg, Hickory, Beallsville\nand West Alexander.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.",
                "response": "Avoid",
